xmclock is a clock program for X that keeps metric time.

What's metric time?  In brief, instead of ticking off the day in seconds,
minutes, and hours, you divide the day into 1000 equal units and subdivide
by tens to gain additional accuracy.  For more detailed info and my
reasons for doing this, see the online help.

Feature list: 	Menu driven
		Selectable accuracy (0,1,2,3 decimal places)
		3 display fontsizes
		Date display (optional)
		Chronograph display (optional)
		Standard 24 hour time display (optional)
		Alarm
		Killable menu (keyboard commands to quit or bring it back)
		xmclock help online
		Metric time reference online
		Dec/Hex/Oct/Bin/ASCII Chart (0-127) online
		Help browser can be used alone to browse text in X
		
xmclock is a proof-of-concept application.  It is not intended to be a
hyperprecise timekeeping tool.  It uses a combination of timing loops
and calls to date to keep load low and maintain accuracy.  You will
need Tk 4.0 or higher to run it.  Enjoy!

