-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


Hmm - sorry for two posts so quickly after each other.
I changed my mind and fixed all bugs in cfdisk that people
have complained to me about.  Then, those that prevented
cfdisk from working on each of my disks.

So, new release, entirely untested, except that it is able
to list the partitions on my disks: cfdisk-0.8f.

Main changes:
- - llseek is called correctly, so that it works on large disks
- - various rather common layouts of logical partitions are no
  longer rejected
- - in a handful of places, the computation of the starting offset
  of a partition has been corrected - there could easily be more
  places where similar bugs still need fixing
- - DOS partitions are now listed together with their volume label,
  making it easier for people from the DOS-world to connect
  the Linux hda2 and hda5 to their DOS partitions.
  [I considered adding C:, D: etc, but that is difficult, since
   DOS, W3.11, W95, WNT, OS/2 all have slightly different
   naming schemes for these disks.]
- - layout adapted to larger disks
- - cfdisk is willing to work in read-only mode

Site: ftp.win.tue.nl:/pub/linux/util/cfdisk-0.8f.tar.gz

Complaints to aeb@cwi.nl

Andries

