After being on low priority for too long I have now restarted the Linux
User Group list.

	History:

I started this list about a year ago ang got overwhelming responses. The
list grew quickly and I had to find people to help me out. After some
time I found coworkers in the USA, UK and Australia. They assisted and
took the list to a higher level. But it didn't last too long. One by one
the coworkers couldn't put enough effort in it or were just plain
unreachable.

As the other maintainers failed to respond or had to change priorities I
decided that all entries should go through a form to simplify the work.
However creating this form was not on my top priority list. But with
some help I managed to get a decent form and I am happy to restart the
list and I hope that it may prosper and be a good guide to help people
find other people that like Linux and may be able to help.

	Actions:

I call upon all of you to help me out so this list may benifit the whole
of the Linux community.

 1.	Anyone having references to http://www.nllgg.nl/LUGWW/ or any
subdirectory of that please remove that old reference as the files are
gone. The current home base is: http://www.nllgg.nl/lugww/ which is a
single file for the moment. It may split into other files as needed.

 2.	Any Linux User Group should take a look and fill in the form so
people in the area may find you. Entries will be handled as fast as I
can for the coming weeks. I hope to do them at least daily during
startup.

 3.	Any would be mirror sites have a look in a week or two and see if
this is a nice thing to have on your site. Contact me after the list has
actually started to get some volume so I can attend to the mirror
aspects of it. This may take a little work yet so give me untill halfway
May to get things sorted out.

	Thanks:

Thanks for the fellow NLLGG webmasters for getting this script working.
Thanks to all of you who did help and participate in the first list. 

Thanks,
Hugo.

