I write visualisation-tool for the EIB-instabus (http://www.eiba.com).

the eib is a home automatisation system for private and home installation.
You put actors and sensor together with a two wire cable and program the
components and then you can switch your lights, radiator and so far.

Because theres only a tools for dos and windows  for visualisation buildings,
I write a program, running undr X and Linux to look your ligths in your house.

The first release is tested and I'm looking for people to test the
packet in a big EIB network.

The Software reads the EIB-Bus and write the actions in a logfile.
xeib is the visualisation and you can see on your X-Window different
icons for on and off ceilings etc.

You can start more than one xeib at the same server.


Because there's a extremly hard- & softwarehandshake at older EIB-Businterfaces
(older than 2.0), you need a router. I have used an old DOS-PC, it's only
necessary to have two serial ports. Connect EIB at COM1, the UNIX at COM2,
boot a DOS and start router.exe. (who can send me a new Businterface? )

contact: joku@stud.uni-sb.de
