-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

This is to announce a new alpha version, 6.8.0a4 of taper.
Taper is a user friendly backup program that supports floppies,
floppy drive connected tape drives, SCSI tape drives, removable
devices (eg. IOMEGA ZIP) as well as regular files.

The major change in this version is the capability to use networked
drives like tar (eg. myhost.com:/dev/tape). Disk space usage for 
the info file has been reduced by eliminating one of the index
files. Processing of the info file before restore is much quicker
and selecting of files in restore is much quicker. A few other
bug fixes as well.



Begin3
Title:		Taper
Version:  	6.8.0a4
Entered-date:	20apr97
Description:	This is a tape backup and restore program that provides
		a friendly user interface to allow backing/restoring
		files to a tape drive. Alternatively, files can be backed
		up to hard disk files. Selecting files for backup and restore
	 	is very similar to the Mouseless Commander interface and
		allows easy traversal of directories. Recursively selected
		directories are supported. Incremental backup and automatic
		most recent restore are defaults settings. SCSI, ftape,
		zftape, and removable drives are supported (ide tape drives
		in ALPHA stage)
		Information about archives is stored on the hard disk 
		allowing information about  archives to be obtained without
		having to have the tape in the drive. 
			Web Page: www.multiline.com.au/~yusuf
Keywords:	Tape, Backup, Archive
Author:		yusuf@multiline.com.au (yusuf nagree)
Maintained-by:	yusuf@multiline.com.au
Primary-site:	sunsite.unc.edu  /pub/Linux/system/backup/taper-6.8.0a4.tar.gz
		tsx-11.mit.edu /pub/linux/sources/sbin/taper-6.8.0a4.tar.gz
		Also available from web page
		Approx 310K
Platforms:	linux > 1.2.1
		ncurses >= 1.9.6 with the forms library
		GCC > 2.6.1 
Copying-policy:	GPL
End



Cheers, Yusuf
