DISLIN is a high-level and easy to use graphics library for displaying
data as curves, bar graphs, pie charts, 3D-colour plots, surfaces,
contours and maps. Several output formats are supported such as X11,
PostScript, CGM, HPGL, TIFF and Prescribe. The library contains about
400 plotting and parameter setting routines and is available for several C,
Fortran 77 and Fortran 90 compilers.

A free version of DISLIN for the Linux NAG f90 compiler is available from

          ftp://ftp.gwdg.de/pub/grafik/dislin

and from the DISLIN Home Page

          http://www.mpae.gwdg.de/dislin/dislin.html

The Linux files are:

      dislin_manual.63.tar.gz          DISLIN PostScript manual
      unix/dislin_linux.63.tar.gz      DISLIN for gcc, g77 and f2c, Utilities
      unix/dislin_linux_f90.63.tar.gz  DISLIN for NAG f90 compiler
      unix/dislin_linux_F.63.tar.gz    DISLIN for Linux Imagine F compiler
      unix/README.UNX                  Installation instructions

