For Immediate Release:

BLACKMAIL INTERNET MAIL FILTER PROXY
For users of SMAIL and QMAIL
This distribution is *FREE*, released under GPL

        Tired of receiving spam from bogus Internet sites?  Is the
        taste of moldy, overbloated spam getting to you?  Look no
        further, friends, BlackMail is here to save your troubles
        and cure your mail headaches.

        Bitgate Software has just released BlackMail 0.22, a do-all,
        see-all, filter-all mail proxy that filters mail by domain,
        by header, and yes friends, by command.

        If you're running sendmail, you shouldn't need this package,
        but for those of us running smail and qmail, this package is
        ideal.  It's great fun for the entire family.  Your kids,
        pets, and relatives will love this one.

        What does it do?  I'm glad you asked.  Here's a small listing
        of just some of the things it can filter:

        o) MAIL FROM commands are filtered to check top level domains.
        o) HELO commands are filtered to check top level domains, and
           a listing of sites that you have filtered out.
        o) RCPT TO commands are filtered to check top level domains,
           and to make sure the recipient matches a user on your
           system.  If not, it is treated as a mail forwarding attempt,
           and is immediately discarded with a bogus error to confuse
           the other mailer.
        o) Mail headers are filtered by:
           Received (The standard release automatically checks for any
                     mail from Cyber Promotions, and discards it.)
           From, X-From, X-Apparently-From, *From* (!!)
           To, Reply-To, X-To, X-Send-To, *To* (!!)
           X-UIDL (Follows RFC1939 checks on UIDL entries, and will soon
                   check palindromic sequences in the UIDL for fakes.)

        Filters can be easily added, but they need to be hard-coded.
        The source is provided for those of you hackers who want to
        add more filtering agents to the source.

        I ask that if you run SMAIL or QMAIL, that you carefully consider
        running BlackMail.  Autobahn Internet runs it, and you should
        run it.  It will cure all your problems dealing with spam.  It
        will make you and your customers very happy.

        Together, we can fight unwanted Internet Spam!  For those of
        you interested in helping with the project, please tune your
        Web Browsers to http://www.bitgate.com/spam/.

- -- Ken Hollis


