Pileup is a program which simulates a Morse Code pileup. 
It uses multiple voices of a SoundBlaster (or compatible) card to
simulate a specified number of Morse Code stations. The program
varies the speed, volume and frequency of the Morse Code stations in
correctly order to simulate a pileup.

Pileup is based on sccw by Steve Merrifield (sjm@ee.latrobe.edu.au).

What's new in v1.1:
- --------------------

o Added an interactive competition mode where each callsign copied is
  entered into the keyboard and scored. At the end of the run the list
  of transmitted and received calls is displayed. I am maintaining a
  High Score list at "http://www.babbage.demon.co.uk/hiscores.html";

o Uses LinuxThreads.

Download
- --------

o ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming/pileup-1.1.tar.gz
  This will hopefully be moved to
  ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/apps/ham/morse/pileup-1.1.tar.gz

o Pileup home page
  http://www.babbage.demon.co.uk/pileup.html

pileup v1.1 LSM
- ---------------

