SmartUPS 1.0 for Un*x
- ---------------------
I had access to a UPS (the box says made in Taiwan, but it has a 
Grinaker (who makes mining equipment in South-Africa) stricker) and a
computer with "Safeware plus" software installed, so I hooked up the
scope to see how the protocol between the computer and the UPS worked.
Then I decided that Linux should also have software to plot the voltages
etc. I wrote the UPS daemon that talks to the UPS and signals to init
when there is a power problem, or when the power comes back on. When it
receives a TERM signal during the shutdown process, it will tell the UPS
to kill the power after 30 seconds. It also listens for TCP connections
and outputs the statistics in ASCII format.

I wrote a general purpose graphing program that gets its data using
TCP sockets and plots it on in an X11 window.

Read the manpage in the package for installation instructions.

I only tested it on one computer (Slackware) and UPS, so please tell me
of any problems.

I uploaded the package to sunsite.unc.edu /incoming/Linux, so it should
be availible as /pub/Linux/system/ups/smartups-1.0.tgz soon, but if it
is not, e-mail me if you want it.

Nic Roets (geo@pta.lia.net)



