What is ifmail?
=============== 
Ifmail is a package that allows a Unix machine to integrate an FTN (fido-like)
network, and act as a gateway between it and usenet and/or e-mail.
It includes the gating software, an areafix, a nodediff patcher, a mailer
and a file-echo manager.

What are "tx" patches so?
=========================
These are diffs against plain 2.9 version that add some functionalities.
I maintain the "tx" diffs from many sources and contributions.

What are the differences ?
==========================
"tx" versions adds charset support, References: managing, support for
different Areas files for different feeds, domain#1:2/34.56 type of
adresses support, support for packet password different than session
password, PGP signed messages support, Vmodem patches applied,
better MSGID/Message-ID managements, 

