Commercial (game):
Last Defender 1.2.0, a.k.a. ldefx, is available now.

You need an X server running at 8bpp, with the DGA or Shm extensions.
For DGA you need a linearly addressable video card or scrolling is not
smooth (after a DGA Bank switch function you have to wait writing to the
screen until a wait retrace has occurred, it seems) and a 640x480 mode
in your XF86Config file. The shared memory version strangely enough is
actually faster than the DGA version! (probably only for a well
accelerated chipset)

The program runs at 320x240, and 640x480. The 640x480 mode is either
pixel doubling or hi-res (text, landscape). BTW, the main colours of
your desktop will not be messed up even though I use a private colour
map (for colour cycling).

Relegation of all drawing routines to separate general framebuffer and
specific drawing routines means porting to GGI should not be difficult
(mail me if you're interested in such a beast).

For smooth scrolling, the program uses a wait_retrace function similar
to the svgalib one. This means the program is currently limited to
running on x86 and alpha systems.

Please contact me if you know how to access the vertical retrace
information on other systems.

Configuration is now taken care of with a script guiding you through all
the options.

For more information see

	http://www.cistron.nl/~wouters/linuxarc.html


Wouter  (wouters@cistron.nl)




