CLUE Newsletter, April 1997
======================================================

CLUE is open to anyone with an interest in Linux.  Whether you are a Unix
   expert or are simply new to Linux and want to learn more about the
   Internet and Operating System phenomena that Linux represents. All 
   interested parties are invited to attend CLUE User Group meetings.

   Let's learn from each other!

The Colorado Linux Users & Enthusiasts (CLUE), normally meets the
   third Thursday of every month. The next meeting will be at
   7:00pm on April 17th, 1997. The location will be Smoky Hill High
   School, located at 16100 E. Smoky Hill Rd. in Southeast
   Aurora.  A software library is available and door prizes
   are available at many meetings.

   CLUE extends its many thanks to Smoky Hill High School and
   their faculty sponsor, Darlene Olguin, for the use of their 
   facilities.

======================================================

This Month's Topic: 
   "Commercial Applications"

   The number of commercial applications available for Linux has
   grown significantly over the past year.  Applications include
   spreadsheets, word processors, CAD tools, and software and Website
   development tools.  This months meeting will focus on the applications
   that are available and where to get them.

======================================================

Notes from March 1997 meeting:

   The March meeting was an open forum to discuss the details of 
   the upcoming installation festival.  

======================================================

Upcoming Events of interest:

  Local
  -----
	None.

  World Wide
  ----------
   DECUS Cincinnati, May 1997. 
   Fourth International Linux Kongress 1997 Wuerzburg, May 1997.

======================================================

Administrivia:

CLUE welcomes members of the Linux User Community to speak at the monthly
   meetings.  Please contact president@clue.denver.co.us to arrange
   your talk.  All speakers are expected to provide a written summary of
   the talk so that we may place it in the newsletter and on our Web site.

CLUE has a home page!  Find us at http://www.clue.denver.co.us.
   Information on getting on or off the CLUE Newsletter mailing list
   is available at this site.
 
CLUE is open to anyone with an interest in Linux.  Whether you are a Unix
   expert or are simply new to Linux and want to learn more about the
   Internet and Operating System phenomena that Linux represents. All 
   interested parties are invited to attend CLUE User Group meetings.

   The CLUE Board of Directors meets immediately after the main Users
   Group meeting to schedule and organize the CLUE meetings and other
   Linux related activities.  The Board meeting is open to the public, 
   but attendees should note anyone who attends may be assigned 
   organizational responsibilities!  Volunteerism is a good thing!

   CLUE is open to and actively seeks cooperative efforts with other
   User Groups in the Colorado Front Range.  Contact
   president@clue.denver.co.us to see what we can do together.

   Let's learn from each other!

======================================================

Directions to Smoky Hill High School:  

   Take Parker south from I-225, to Quincy.  There will be a shopping 
   center on the left, and a Stoplight. Take a left on Quincy. Then the 
   first stoplight with a right turn will be Smoky Hill Road.  Turn
   right onto Smoky Hill, cross Chambers (a light), and then turn right 
   at Laredo (a stop light).  Turn left into the school parking lot at 
   the next light.  Drive towards the end of the school to the Activities
   Entrance which will be the large entrance past the end of the
   portable classrooms.  Enter the building and proceed straight down the 
   wide hall.  You will end up in front of the entrance to the gym.  Turn 
   left and go down the hall to the first hallway on the right.  Turn right 
   and the first classroom on the right, room 814 (the CAD Lab) will be 
   the CLUE meeting room.  There will be signs posted on the Activities 
   Entrance, by the Gym, on the hallway leading to the room and next to the 
   room.

======================================================

This newsletter is compiled by the CLUE Newsletter Editor,
      Michael J. Hammel <mjhammel@csn.net>, 
   who welcomes comments on its form and content.

