Announcing the availability of a Linux port of Quarks, a distributed shared
memory system for PCs.

What is Quarks?

Quarks is a library developed by the University of Utah which allows
you to take a network of computers and turn them into a larger, more
powerful computer.  The library creates the illusion of a shared memory
multiprocessor for applications.

Who it is for?

This should be of interest to people doing mutiprocessing research.
It should also interest hobbyists who have more than one PC on a
network, and want to try creating programs that use the resources of
all of their machines at once.

Where is it?

More information and complete source code (880k tar file) can be found
on the Linux Quarks home page, at:

http://www.eecg.toronto.edu/~colohan/quarks.html. 

===

