Sorry everyone, but patches have become necessary in light of
recent Linux kernels. It is known that at least up to version
2.0.23 that wavplay 1.0 will compile OK. At some release beyond
that revision, you'll want these patches to compile it.

One patch fixes another small problem that only shows itself
on certain WAV files. A shell script is included to apply the
patches to make it easy to install. You must have the patch
command installed on your system however.

This brings wavplay up to release 1.0pl1.

The patches have been uploaded to sunsite.unc.edu. Look for the
file:
	wavplay-1.0.patch1.tar.gz

Please read the file README.PATCH1 first.

Thanks, enjoy!

