ANNOUNCE: Release of version 0.94 of the Netwide Assembler (NASM)
=================================================================

NASM is an 80x86 assembler designed for portability and modularity.
It supports a range of object file formats including Linux a.out and
ELF, COFF, Microsoft 16-bit OBJ and Win32. It will also output plain
binary files. Its syntax is designed to be simple and easy to
understand, similar to Intel's but less complex. It supports
Pentium, P6 and MMX opcodes, and has macro capability. It includes a
disassembler as well.

This release contains the long-awaited macro processor! NASM can now
handle macros, both of the multi-line MASM type and the single-line
C type, and supports multi-level file inclusion, rather than the
single level that was supported previously. In addition, more bugs
have been fixed, notably problems with ELF output, the FDIV and FSUB
instructions, and wrong offset calculations in one very strange
case.

NASM is currently available in Unix .tar.gz format as

  ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/devel/lang/assemblers/nasm-0.94.tar.gz

It's also been posted to Simtel and the Coast-to-Coast Repository in
DOS archive form, and is available from

  ftp://ftp.simtel.net/pub/simtelnet/msdos/asmutl/nasm094.zip
  ftp://ftp.simtel.net/pub/simtelnet/msdos/asmutl/nasm094s.zip
  ftp://ftp.coast.net/coast/msdos/asmutil/nasm094.zip
  ftp://ftp.coast.net/coast/msdos/asmutil/nasm094s.zip

(nasm094s.zip includes source code; nasm094.zip is binaries-only).
Of course these files are also available from any site, such as
sunsite.doc.ic.ac.uk, which mirrors sunsite.unc.edu, Simtel or
Coast.

If you can't get it from any of those, it's also available from my
back-up FTP site, as

  ftp://yoda.trin.cam.ac.uk/pub/simon/nasm-0.94.tar.gz
  ftp://yoda.trin.cam.ac.uk/pub/simon/nasm094.zip
  ftp://yoda.trin.cam.ac.uk/pub/simon/nasm094s.zip

Enjoy using NASM!
