The April 1997 meeting of Washington DC Linux user group will take
place on Wednesday, April 16, 7pm, at the Lippsett auditorium on
the grounds of NIH (see directions below).

We will watch video of Linus Torvalds' talk at the December Usenix,
and discuss recent Linux Expo in North Carolina.

The remaining meeting dates for year 1997 (our usual time---7 pm on
every third Wednesday of each month) are:

May 21, June 18, July 16, August 20, September 17, October 15,
November 19 and December 17

NEWSFLASH

We got so good in running Linux Installfests that several of us (David
Niemi, David Lesher, Don Becker, Eric Youngdale and others) were asked
by RedHat to help them organize and run the Installfest during the
Linux Expo 1997.

Our group was featured in Linux Journal! Your humble president was
interviewed by LJ and the result appeared in the May issue.  Thanks to
the good work and persistence of everyone, we are considered one of
the more successfull Linux groups. 


