      SAL  Beta Release Announcement

What is SAL ?
=============

SAL's (Scientific Applications on Linux) web page is a collection of
information and links of software (from public domain to commercial and
anything in between) that scientists and engineers will be interested in.
This broad coverage of Linux applications will also benefit the whole Linux
community. This popular site was created in 1995 and now, we at Kachina
Technologies, Inc. have developed a new version of SAL to serve Linux users
better.

URL ?
=====

USA ---
     http://SAL.KachinaTech.COM
     (Note: the original text-based SAL will be still available through
     http://www.KachinaTech.COM/SAL/linux_prg.html through the beta testing
     phase. However, no further maintanence will be performed.)

Mirrors ---
     Germany: http://ftp.llp.fu-berlin.de/lsoft/
     Italy: http://chpc06.ch.unito.it/linux/

Copyright and Distribution of SAL ?
===================================

SAL is copyrighted by Dr. Herng-Jeng Jou and Kachina Technologies, Inc. and
it can be freely redistributed under GPL version 2 or later, otherwise
stated by their respective owners. We recommend not to redistribute it until
the beta testing is done.

What's in SAL beta ?
====================

To give you an idea of what topics are in SAL now, the following are the
categories of SAL:

Mathematics
   * Computer Algebra Systems   * Array-Oriented & Linear Algebra Systems
   * Statistics                 * Number Theory                 * Misc

Numerical Analysis
   * Source Code Repositories   * Discrete Methods & Related Tools
   * Misc

Parallel Computing
   * Programming Languages and Systems       * Communication Libraries
   * Tools and Utilities                     * Misc

Scientific Data Processing & Visualization
   * Software Packages             * Libraries

Computer Graphics, Images & Signals
   * Processing & Visualization          * CAD, Drawing & Painting Tools
   * Modelers                            * Raytracers
   * Image Viewer, Conversions & Manipulations
   * Geographic Information Systems      * Misc

Programming
   * Languages & Compilers                * Tools & Utilities
   * GL(TM)/OpenGL(TM) Related Libraries & Toolkits
   * Other Graphic Libraries              * X11 Libraries & Toolkits

Office Software
   * Office Suites                        * Typesetting & Formatting
   * Word Processing & Publishing         * Spreadsheets

Other Scientific Fields
   * Electrical & Related Software        * Chemistry, Biology & Related
   * Misc

Would you like to be a beta tester ?
====================================

Everyone can be a beta tester without any obligation or registration. All
you need to do is surf SAL and find errors or offer suggestions, and then
let us know. SAL especially welcomes the following information:

   * Are all links correct? Can you find the new URL for broken links in
     SAL?
   * Typos? Grammatical errors?
   * New contributions to SAL?
   * Debian and/or RedHat binary packages information?
   * If you have used any software mentioned in SAL, would you like to offer
     some User Comments to that software (anonymously if you like)?
   * Misplaced software which should belong to other sections? Or should
     have a link in other sections?
   * What other sections you would like to see in SAL? (For example, how
     about an Text Editors section in SAL?)
   * Any other ideas you can offer.

What's new in SAL beta ?
========================

   * New topic categorizing scheme, as shown above, hopefully will ease the
     pain when looking for the software you like.
   * Search engine.
   * New web page design (without frame and non-graphic friendly).
   * Expanded information in each software package, and expanded repository.
   * SAL team will try to maintain close contact with the software authors,
     so that we always have as up-to-date information displayed as possible.
     We understand that it is very frustrating when one finds a software
     useful but the link is broken.
   * SAL belongs to the Linux community and all Linux Lovers are welcome to
     make contributions to it. There is a user feedback form and please
     don't forget to fill it out when you visit SAL. We'd like to hear from
     you!

Final Words
===========

The new SAL beta took us longer to release than expected because of the
amount of work involved --- setting up categories, placing software in
correct sections, verifying/correcting links, designing web page structure,
search engines, gathering more information, contacting authors and revising
the pages.

We sincerely hope SAL will be helpful to the Linux community and helps
promote the usage of Linux in the Scientific/Engineering arena. Please tell
us whether you like the new SAL or not, and certainly, SAL is not perfect
so, we welcome every Linux Lover's comments.

SAL Team, SAL@KachinaTech.COM
Kachina Technologies, Inc.


