tcharge version 1.2
- -------------------
`Tcharge' is a small X program for watching the time a telephone
connection is up and to have an eye on the charges to be payed for the
connection. An ("analog") clock displays the time and a textfield
monitors the charge. A possibility for making further statitistics is
provided.
It's very easy to add support for your phone company even without
programming knowledge (e.g. take into account provider charges...)

The highlights of changes since version 1.0:
Tcharge..
 now supports `per second billing' (e.g. for USA, UK)
 now supports the following countries/phone companies:
  Germany, France, Japan, Portugal, Slovenia, Hungary, Belgium, Swiss,
  Italy, Netherlands, South Africa, Spain and the UK.
 now may look for the existance of a given file (e.g. a pidfile of the
  dialing demon) and start/stop charge computing when it is
  created/deleted.
 now may set of a little alarm some seconds before a new unit begins
 now knows about public holidays
 now supports ISDN
not to notice a lot of further improvements and bug fixes.

