I have uploaded to sunsite.unc.edu a port to Linux of ren, a small
utility (originally written by Vladimir Lanin in 1988) allowing renaming
of multiple files in the current directory with a single command, which
can not be done directly with mv.  Those who tend to make typing errors
in things like
ls -d *.new | sed 's/\(.*\)\.new$/mv & \1.old/' | sh
can now do simply
ren "*.new" #1.old

