Ladies and Gentlemen,

this is a reminder that the Linux CD Giveaway List at

    http://emile.math.ucsb.edu:8000/giveaway.html

is still going strong. If you have a spare Linux CD to give away or if
you would be willing to lend a Linux CD locally, please consider
adding yourself to the list so that more people can be won for Linux,
especially in parts of the world where Linux CDs are not yet readily
available.

Here is how it works: you put your email address on the list, an
interested party contacts you, then sends you a self-addressed stamped
envelope, you put the CD in and send it off.

Please note that some huge computations have been started on emile
recently and sometimes the web server does not respond because of that
(Solaris -- what can you expect?) Just try again later.

If you are new to Linux and would like to have a free Linux CD, check
out the above URL as well. If you have a poor connection, you can also
get the Giveaway List via email by sending mail like so:
    To: boldt@math.ucsb.edu
    Subject: send giveaway_list


Best regards,
