-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


tplay is a POSIX-threaded audio player especially coded 
for use with MPEG-decoders. These decoders take typically
a lot of CPU-time so some kind of buffer between decoder
and audio device is needed to reduce clipping during
CPU usage peaks.

This program is still evolving and thus considered as
BETA. 

Available at:

http://www.iki.fi/i/tplay.html
ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/apps/sound/players/tplay-0.1.tar.gz

