The next monthly meeting of the Free Unix Users of New Mexico
will be held Saturday, April 12, 1996 at the Farris Engineering
Center at the University of New Mexico in Albuquerque from
4:30 to 6:00.  This group is oriented toward the freely available
Unixes (Linux, FreeBSD, NetBSD, OpenBSD, GNU Hurd, or VsTA) and
anyone with interest in these operating systems is invited to
attend.

This month, we will have an "Installation Assistance Day."  There
will be IP addresses and connections available for network installs
(for those with ethernet cards), and CD's for those with CDROM
drives.

We will meet in the computer science conference room, room 141,
which is near the NW corner of the Farris building.  The building's
main entrance is on the East side of the building and is usually
open.  If it is not, the entrance on the North side of the building
will be open.

We have a maillist at

	fuunm@astro.phys.unm.edu

which can be subscribed to by mailing to

	fuunm-request@astro.phys.unm.edu

and ask to be put on the FUUNM maillist.


