-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


Hello all,

I spent some time this month beefing up cdda2wav0.8's ability to cope
with Imperfect Reality.  I'd like to announce the release of the
Paranoia II patch against cdda2wav0.8 (incrementing the version to
0.86) for testing, but it is probably ready for general use.
Specifically, if cdda2wav produces samples with clicks and pops on
your machine, or is constantly bailing with 'sync error' messages,
this version is for you.

Heiko (author of cdda2wav) is evaluating whether or not the Paranoia
II patch is to be incorporated in the mainstream release of cdda2wav;
I'd like to get in more testing before then.

>From README.paranoia:

"All CDROM drives are not created equal.  You're probably using this
patch because yours is a little less equal than others-- or maybe you
just keep your CD collection in a box of full of gravel.  Jewel cases
are for wimps; you know what I'm talking about.

This patch adds extra-robust interframe syncronization, code to detect
scratches (and hold sync across the scratch) and finally routines to
filter out scratches as best possible.  These are all handled
automatically by fairly modular code."

The patch to 0.8 may be found at :
http://web.mit.edu/afs/sipb/user/xiphmont/cdda2wav/cdda2wav0.86-paranoiaII.patch.gz

The complete source with patch already applied is at:
http://web.mit.edu/afs/sipb/user/xiphmont/cdda2wav/cdda2wav0.86-paranoiaII.src.tgz

Note that bugs in this version should be reported to me
(xiphmont@mit.edu) and not Heiko.  Also, read README and
README.paranoia carefully before reporting trouble.

Thanks and happy hacking,
Monty
xiphmont@mit.edu



