-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


Every once in a while, somebody in c.o.l.networking will ask if it's possible 
to share a modem hanging off a Linux box with other machines running Windows 
or some Unix.

Mserver is a package that does just that. The main program is the server, but
it also contains a small client for Unix platforms. (For a Windows client,
look for a program called "COMt" or anything offering similar functionality)

The server supports any number of modems served through a single TCP port
and allows you to configure any number of TCP ports serving modems. It also
allows you to restrict clients based on wildcarded IP addresses or hostnames.

Mserver 0.21 is available from :

	ftp://ftp.innet.be/pub/staff/carl/mserver-0.21.tar.gz

carl.





